From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:53:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 103/117] drm/msm/dp: exit the PHY when the DP controller
 runtime suspends

The DP controller loses its state while the display subsystem is powered
off. Runtime suspend deinitializes the controller but exits the PHY only
for eDP, so for DP the PHY stays marked initialized, the next plug does
not set it up again and every AUX transfer times out: a monitor plugged
in while the screen is off hangs its detection.

A DP controller only runtime suspends with no sink attached, so exit the
PHY for DP as well; detection and the plug path initialize it again.

Found by Reixo0, commit fcd65ba21d8c ("drm/msm/dp: let the PHY go when the
DP controller suspends") in github Reixo0/linux (no Signed-off-by);
re-implemented.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 0449571cbd639..8b85476d31b71 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -1592,10 +1592,16 @@ static int msm_dp_pm_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 
 	disable_irq(dp->irq);
 
-	if (dp->msm_dp_display.is_edp) {
-		msm_dp_display_host_phy_exit(dp);
+	/*
+	 * The controller loses its state while the display subsystem is
+	 * powered off (screen off). Exit the PHY for DP as for eDP: left
+	 * marked initialized, it would not be set up again on the next plug
+	 * and every AUX transfer would time out. DP only runtime suspends
+	 * with no sink attached; detection and the plug path init it again.
+	 */
+	msm_dp_display_host_phy_exit(dp);
+	if (dp->msm_dp_display.is_edp)
 		msm_dp_aux_hpd_disable(dp->aux);
-	}
 	msm_dp_display_host_deinit(dp);
 
 	return 0;
